# User Login Feature Specification

## 1. Overview
The user login feature allows registered users to authenticate into the system using their email and password.

## 2. Functional Requirements

### 2.1 Login Form
- System shall display login form with email and password fields
- Email field must accept valid email format
- Password field must be masked with asterisks
- "Login" button to submit credentials
- "Forgot Password" link for password recovery

### 2.2 Authentication Process
1. User enters email and password
2. System validates email format
3. System checks if account exists
4. System verifies password matches stored hash
5. If successful, redirect to dashboard
6. If failed, display appropriate error message

### 2.3 Validation Rules
- Email: Must be valid format, max 255 characters
- Password: Must be 8-32 characters, alphanumeric with special chars
- Both fields are required

### 2.4 Error Handling
- Invalid email format: "Please enter a valid email address"
- Account not found: "No account found with this email"
- Wrong password: "Incorrect password. Please try again"
- Account locked: "Your account has been locked. Please contact support"
- Server error: "Unable to process login. Please try again later"

### 2.5 Security Requirements
- Password transmission over HTTPS only
- Maximum 5 failed login attempts, then lock account for 30 minutes
- Session timeout after 2 hours of inactivity
- JWT token for session management

## 3. Edge Cases
- Empty email or password fields
- SQL injection attempts in email field
- XSS attempts in input fields
- Concurrent login attempts from same account
- Login during system maintenance

## 4. Success Criteria
- User can successfully login with correct credentials
- Appropriate error messages for all failure scenarios
- Session properly created and managed
- Failed login attempts tracked and enforced
- Browser compatibility: Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge (latest versions)

## 5. New Feature - Two-Factor Authentication
- User can enable 2FA for enhanced security
- Supports SMS and authenticator app

## 6. Updated Requirements
- Password policy updated: minimum 10 characters (changed from 8)